# review.md and review-change.md say what the enrollment review and the change review check
# (.github/workflows/build.yaml reads main's copies), and .claude/skills/write-to-maintainer/ says how every message to
# a maintainer is written and checked. The ruleset of main requires a code owner's approval, so a change to any of
# them, or to this file, which says who owns them, needs the approval of a member of @theorem-labs/engineering, a team
# of people. No other file has an owner, so no other pull
# request needs a code owner. These lines stay the last patterns of the file: the last pattern that matches a file
# decides its owner.
/review.md @theorem-labs/engineering
/review-change.md @theorem-labs/engineering
/.claude/skills/write-to-maintainer/ @theorem-labs/engineering
/.github/CODEOWNERS @theorem-labs/engineering
